#![no_std]

//! QMI protocol codec.
//!
//! The wire format runtime lives in this crate root; the per-service message
//! and TLV types under [`types`] are generated by `cargo xtask qmi-codegen`
//! from the QMI service database in `data/`.
//!
//! Requests are sent from the [`Session`] that [`QmiClient::with_session`]
//! hands out, with one of the generated request types: the [`Request`] trait
//! that request implements carries the service, the message id and the
//! response type, and its response points back at it.
//!
//! Every response carries a `Result` TLV, and the rest of the answer only
//! means something when that says the request succeeded. A generated response
//! is therefore the data of a success: [`Session::call`] hands it back
//! directly and reports a request the modem rejected as the protocol error it
//! was answered with.
//!
//! The client is generic over its transport, so the same protocol code runs
//! over a USB CDC WDM function ([`UsbQmiClient`]) and over QRTR
//! ([`QrtrTransport`]), which is what [`Multiplexing`] tells it apart by.

